  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The dimensions of universal constant $G$, is obtained by Newton's law of gravitation<br />$F=\\frac{G m_{1} m_{2}}{r^{2}}$<br />$\\begin{array}{l}<br />G=\\frac{F \\times r^{2}}{m_{1} m_{2}} \\\\<br />F=\\text { Force }<br />\\end{array}$<br />$r=$ Distance $m_{1}$ and $m_{2}$ are masses<br />$\\begin{aligned}<br />G &=\\frac{\\left[M^{1} L^{1} T^{-2}\\right]\\left[L^{2}\\right]}{[M][M]} \\\\<br />&=\\frac{\\left[M^{\\prime} L^{2} T^{-2}\\right]}{\\left[M^{2}\\right]}=\\left[M^{-1} L^{2} T^{-2}\\right]<br />\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
